# Frontend invariants

## Backend access — never direct

The frontend talks to FastAPI **only** through the Next.js rewrite at `/api/backend/*` (configured in `frontend/next.config.ts`). The browser never sees the backend origin directly. `BACKEND_URL` env var controls the rewrite target.

All HTTP calls go through `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`. Do not introduce `fetch()` calls to the backend from components.

## Hand-written types mirror

`frontend/src/lib/types.ts` is **hand-written** to mirror the Pydantic schemas in `backend/src/autotasker_backend/schemas/`. Phase 2 will generate this from the FastAPI OpenAPI schema. **Until then, keep them in sync manually whenever a schema changes.**

When you change a Pydantic model, update the corresponding TypeScript interface in the same change.

## SSE event contract

`frontend/src/lib/api.ts::streamForge()` is an async generator that parses SSE frames into `ForgeEvent`s. The event shapes are union-typed in `types.ts` and produced in `backend/src/autotasker_backend/api/chat.py::_stream_architect`. **These two files must stay in sync.**

`forge-chat.tsx` consumes the SSE stream and renders both a chat bubble list and a "pipeline rail" showing each graph node as it executes. Pattern-match on the discriminated `ForgeEvent.type` field — never narrow by checking for property existence.

## TypeScript strict mode

- `tsconfig.json` has `strict: true` and `experimental.typedRoutes: true`.
- Route props and `<Link href={...}>` must use the `Route` type from `next` — string literals will fail typecheck.
- No `any`. No `@ts-ignore`. Prefer `unknown` and narrow.

## Shadcn UI primitives

Components in `src/components/ui/` are vendored Shadcn primitives — do not modify their structure beyond cosmetic class changes. New shared components go in `src/components/`. Use `cn(...)` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging.

## Server vs client components

- Page files (`app/**/page.tsx`) are **Server Components** by default. Keep them small — they should mostly compose Client Components.
- Components that touch React state, browser APIs, or call `streamForge()` must declare `"use client"` at the top of the file.
- Never call `getSupabaseBrowser()` from a Server Component.
